Hmmm.  Forgive me if I'm wrong but I THINK NOT.  My kendo classes never
had me use a PAIR of swords.  The Katana is a TWO handed sword designed
for hacking things apart.  The Wakizashi is a short sword which was
typically used for seppeku, not for "florentine fencing".  Also,
Leonardo uses a pair of ninja-to, a short STRAIGHT japanese sword. 
They've been referred to as Katana on occasion and are poorly
illustrated, but check closely.  Leo doesn't have a Diasho pair as both
blades are the SAME LENGTH.

I hope that I didn't come off sounding too cocky or rude, but it is late
at night and I'm trying to be brief.

I _do_ kind of like the concept of two weapons though.  Perhaps the
thief class should fight Florentine with a rapier and a dagger, striking
twice every time he attacks?  Or how about a new class that has
Florentine as his intrinsic:

MUSKETEER!  Starts with a rapier, a dagger a leather hat and a cape. 
Attacks twice in melee (if armed with a one-handed sword, dagger
combination).  He should be chaotic if he like the Three Musketeers!

Any of the Dev Team feel like making a new character?

